{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "סמך שוכב עם בהמה לאשת אביו", :translit "samakh shokhev im behemah le'esheet aviv", :gloss "adjacent: lies with an animal — his father's wife"} {:he "כבהמה", :translit "kev'hemah", :gloss "like an animal"} {:he "תדירים עמו", :translit "tadirim imo", :gloss "regularly with him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut parshiyot: the adjacent placement of Torah passages signals a thematic link — here, proximity to forbidden partners and opportunity."}], :frame {:text "The hermeneutic principle of smikhut parshiyot derives legal or moral lessons from the juxtaposition of adjacent passages or topics. Rashi on Deuteronomy 27:21 similarly notes that the Torah places 'his father's wife' next to 'lies with an animal' to signal constant domestic proximity. The pattern of the Torah juxtaposing forbidden relations to convey warnings about access is discussed in Sifrei Deuteronomy 282 and Baba Batra 13b regarding adjacency of topics.", :sources ["Rashi on Deuteronomy 27:21" "Sifrei Deuteronomy 282" "Baba Batra 13b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מכה רעהו בסתר", :translit "makeh re'ehu baseter", :gloss "strikes his fellow in secret"} {:he "כמו זנות חותנתו ואחותו", :translit "k'mo zenut choteneto va'chototo", :gloss "like the relations with his mother-in-law and his sister"} {:he "בצנעה בביתו", :translit "b'tzin'ah b'veito", :gloss "in secrecy in his house"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut parshiyot: the word 'in secret' (בסתר) links the two adjacent passages — striking in secret parallels illicit relations conducted in private."}], :frame {:text "The principle of smikhut parshiyot draws connections between adjacent Torah passages. Here the Ba'al HaTurim links 'strikes his fellow in secret' to the preceding prohibited-relations passages, since both involve acts done בסתר, in concealment. The method of deriving lessons from adjacency is treated in Baba Batra 13b and applied by Rashi throughout the Torah.", :sources ["Baba Batra 13b" "Rashi on Deuteronomy 27:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut parshiyot: the adjacent placement of Torah passages signals a thematic link — here, proximity to forbidden partners and opportunity.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Smikhut parshiyot: the word 'in secret' (בסתר) links the two adjacent passages — striking in secret parallels illicit relations conducted in private.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:53.469074270Z", :model "glm-5.2"}